diff --git a/docs/plugins/hooks/messages.md b/docs/plugins/hooks/messages.md
index f56041d72..368f39228 100644
--- a/docs/plugins/hooks/messages.md
+++ b/docs/plugins/hooks/messages.md
@@ -10,6 +10,18 @@ sidebarTitle: "Messages"
 
 Inbound interception, reply takeover, and outbound delivery policy. Part of the [Plugin hooks](/plugins/hooks) guide.
 
+## Select an existing inbound session
+
+Hosts exposing `api.runtime.channel.routing.inboundRouteContractVersion === 1` call `resolve_inbound_route` after provider authorization and before session admission. Slack uses this seam for ordinary messages and routed interaction system events. Return `undefined` to retain the native route, `{ agentId, sessionKey, expectedSessionId, reason? }` to select a concrete existing session, or `{ drop: { reason } }` to stop delivery. A drop is terminal; expired controls must not fall through to another session.
+
+The event includes the admitted `channel`, `accountId`, `workspaceId`, `conversationId`, `senderId`, `messageId`, `content`, and `isDirect`, plus the default `agentId`/`sessionKey`. Optional `replyToId`, `threadId`, `signal`, and `interaction` fields describe explicit references and interactive callbacks. Interaction facts can include `kind`, `messageTs`, `actionId`, `viewId`, `callbackId`, `reference`, and `privateMetadata`. Treat message text and callback data as untrusted evidence. Honor the cancellation signal and keep classification bounded.
+
+`expectedSessionId` identifies the exact lifecycle generation, not a session key alias. The host guards metadata recording and actual agent admission against archive, deletion, and reset. Routing preserves the native attachment, transcript, queue, and source reply delivery paths. It does not grant the caller new sender authorization.
+
+For outbound correlation, `message_sent` contexts may include trusted `agentId`, `sessionKey`, `sessionId`, `workspaceId`, and `conversationId`. `ctx.channelId` remains the provider name, such as `slack`; `ctx.conversationId` is the provider-confirmed Slack conversation. Slack emits an observation for each identified message in aggregate receipts, including committed chunks preceding a later send failure. Identity fields remain optional for sends without an originating session. Never reconstruct a concrete generation from a reused session key after delivery.
+
+Slack plugin interactive handlers receive `interaction.kind: "options"` for external-select suggestions and `interaction.query` from Slack's `block_suggestion.value`. Answer using `respond.options` or `respond.acknowledge` synchronously. Each request needs its own response, including repeated queries. Prepared modals can use `respond.openModal` during a button callback; trigger credentials stay inside the host handler. Native approval controls retain their own policy.
+
 ## Message hooks
 
 For inbound interception, `before_dispatch` receives the incoming message
